---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { getScreenshot } from '../data/screenshots';
import { splitLocale } from '../i18n/routes.mjs';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import IosDownload from '../components/IosDownload.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import { iosQuestions } from '../data/faq';
import { DEVELOPER_URL, APP_STORE_AVAILABLE, IOS_APP_STORE_AVAILABLE, STORAGE_SAVER_TRIO_URL } from '../consts';

const { locale } = splitLocale(Astro.url.pathname);
const overview = getScreenshot('diskpress-for-files-overview', locale);
const selection = getScreenshot('diskpress-for-files-selection', locale);
const results = getScreenshot('diskpress-for-files-results', locale);
const automation = getScreenshot('diskpress-for-files-automation', locale);
const cleanup = getScreenshot('diskpress-for-files-cleanup', locale);
const filecopy = getScreenshot('diskpress-for-files-filecopy', locale);
---
<SiteLayout title="DiskPress for Files - Compression and deduplication" description={`${IOS_APP_STORE_AVAILABLE ? '' : 'Available soon. '}Compress and deduplicate supported local files on iPhone and iPad. Keep every duplicate while sharing its data. Add optional cleanup and Apple Shortcuts workflows.`}>
  <section class="ios-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="ios-heading">
    <div class="product-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">DiskPress for Files for iPhone &amp; iPad</p>
      <h1 id="ios-heading">Your files.<br /><span>A smaller footprint.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Compress and deduplicate supported local files without changing their contents. Duplicate files remain separate while sharing their stored data on the same APFS volume.</p>
      <p>The same native compression and deduplication engine as DiskPress for Mac, made for iPhone and iPad. Open your files normally. No archives to unpack.</p>
      <p>Optimize a selection once, keep your favorite folders ready, or build a workflow with <a href="#shortcuts">Apple Shortcuts</a>. Shortcuts actions start with iOS 16, with background folder actions and compressed file copies on iOS 27.</p>
      <IosDownload />
      <p class="fine">For local files in the Files app, not photo or video optimization. Your Photos library, cloud storage, and protected paths are not supported. <a href="#supported-files">See what is supported</a>.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#platforms">Compare with DiskPress for Mac</a>
    </div>
    <figure class="ios-hero-visual">
      <Image src={overview} alt="DiskPress for Files Overview on iPhone Duo showing available storage, compression and deduplication savings, and Optimize All." widths={[360, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 600px) 240px, (max-width: 780px) 320px, (max-width: 900px) 280px, 320px" format="webp" quality={85} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      <figcaption>Actual app screenshot with example data. Your savings will vary.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="ios-workflow">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A deliberate, local workflow</p><h2>Choose your files.<br />Make a little more room.</h2><p class="lead">Select a supported local folder or individual files. Review the selection, choose your optimization mode, and start when you are ready.</p></div>
      <div class="ios-feature-grid two-up">
        <article class="product-card"><h3>Keep duplicates. Share their data.</h3><p>Deduplication keeps both files and stores identical data once on the same compatible APFS volume. Each file keeps its name and path. File metadata still takes some space, and editing one file does not change the other.</p><a class="text-link" href="/faq/#clones-vs-hard-links">Understand clone sharing</a></article>
        <article class="product-card"><h3>A choice for each folder</h3><p>Choose compression, deduplication, or both for each folder. Optional cleanup can run first with a profile you select. Optimize one saved location or include it in Optimize All.</p></article>
        <article class="product-card"><h3>Settings that fit your files</h3><p>Set exclusions, minimum savings, file size limits, recent-file protection, and performance preferences. Keep unsuitable files out of the work and focus on the data worth optimizing.</p></article>
        <article class="product-card"><h3>Follow every run</h3><p>Watch live file counts and status messages while DiskPress scans, compares, and optimizes. Pause and resume when needed. Results separate new savings from existing savings, and Activity records completed, skipped, and failed operations.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="screenshot-grid ios-screenshot-grid">
        <figure class="screenshot-figure ios-screenshot">
          <figcaption><h3>Choose each folder's workflow</h3><p>Choose one of seven stage combinations and a cleanup profile for each saved location.</p></figcaption>
          <Image src={selection} alt="DiskPress for Files on iPhone Duo showing optimization modes and the selected cleanup profile." widths={[360, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 780px) min(360px, calc(100vw - 98px)), (max-width: 900px) calc(50vw - 98px), 360px" format="webp" quality={85} loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
        <figure class="screenshot-figure ios-screenshot">
          <figcaption><h3>See the result of this run</h3><p>Separate new savings from storage already saved, with counts for compressed, deduplicated, and skipped files.</p></figcaption>
          <Image src={results} alt="DiskPress for Files Results on iPhone Duo showing optimization complete, existing savings, new savings, and file counts." widths={[360, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 780px) min(360px, calc(100vw - 98px)), (max-width: 900px) calc(50vw - 98px), 360px" format="webp" quality={85} loading="lazy" />
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="screenshot-disclaimer">App screenshots use example data. Savings depend on your files and settings.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="cleanup-profiles">
    <div class="ios-hero cleanup-layout">
      <div class="product-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Optional cleanup in 1.2.0</p><h2>Keep rules.<br />Remove clutter.</h2><p>Start with an editable preset for logs or temporary files. Match names or relative paths with wildcard masks or regular expressions, then add keep rules for files and folders you want to protect.</p><p>Choose a removal method for each profile. Permanent deletion cannot be undone. Moving to Trash depends on the selected location and is not available everywhere on iOS. If Trash is unsupported, the item stays in place. Recoverable items may still occupy space.</p><p>To remove logs automatically, choose a cleanup profile for a saved folder and schedule it with Apple Shortcuts. Cleanup runs before any enabled deduplication and compression stages. DiskPress does not continuously monitor folders.</p><a class="text-link" href="/faq/#ios-cleanup">Cleanup on iPhone and iPad</a></div>
      <figure class="ios-hero-visual"><Image src={cleanup} alt="DiskPress for Files cleanup profile editor on iPhone Duo with removal and keep patterns and a per-profile removal method." widths={[360, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 600px) 240px, (max-width: 780px) 320px, (max-width: 900px) 280px, 320px" format="webp" quality={85} loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Editable profiles for the folders you choose.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap" id="shortcuts">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Works with Apple Shortcuts</p><h2>Your folders.<br />Part of your workflow.</h2><p class="lead">Add optimization to a shortcut you run, share, or schedule in Apple's Shortcuts app. DiskPress uses your saved folder settings, including its cleanup profile, enabled stages and exclusions.</p></div>
    <div class="ios-feature-grid two-up">
      <article class="product-card"><p class="eyebrow">iOS and iPadOS 16 or later</p><h3>Start with your saved folders</h3><p>List saved folders and use Start Location Optimization to open DiskPress and begin a run. This action starts the work in the app without waiting for a completion result.</p><p>Open a saved folder's Automation section for Add Location Shortcut and setup help. Build and schedule your workflow in the Shortcuts app.</p></article>
      <article class="product-card"><p class="eyebrow">iOS and iPadOS 27 or later</p><h3>Run a folder in the background</h3><p>Optimize Saved Location runs a saved folder, or a subfolder within it, and returns a completion summary. Optimize Authorized Folder accepts a path inside an already authorized saved location.</p><p>The system may stop background work or require an unlock. These actions do not add continuous monitoring for new or changed files.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="screenshot-grid ios-screenshot-grid">
      <figure class="screenshot-figure ios-screenshot">
        <figcaption><h3>Build a Shortcuts workflow</h3><p>Follow the built-in guidance for saved folders, subfolders, shared shortcuts and file copies.</p></figcaption>
        <Image src={automation} alt="DiskPress for Files Shortcuts guidance on iPhone Duo covering saved folders, subfolders and file copies." widths={[360, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 780px) min(360px, calc(100vw - 98px)), (max-width: 900px) calc(50vw - 98px), 360px" format="webp" quality={85} loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <figure class="screenshot-figure ios-screenshot">
        <figcaption><h3>Return a file to your shortcut</h3><p>Use Compress File Copy on iOS 27 or later with input from another action or a shortcut enabled in the share sheet.</p></figcaption>
        <Image src={filecopy} alt="DiskPress for Files Shortcuts help on iPhone Duo explaining Compress File Copy, share sheet input, and keeping the original file untouched." widths={[360, 720, 1080]} sizes="(max-width: 780px) min(360px, calc(100vw - 98px)), (max-width: 900px) calc(50vw - 98px), 360px" format="webp" quality={85} loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="safety-note"><strong>A shortcut is not a permission grant.</strong> Authorize the local folder in DiskPress first. A path alone never grants access, and sharing a shortcut does not share your folder permissions. Saved locations are more reliable than absolute container paths, which can change.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section workflow-section" id="compressed-copy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Compress File Copy · iOS and iPadOS 27 or later</p><h2>Keep the original.<br />Return a separate copy.</h2><p class="lead">Pass a file from another Shortcuts action or the share sheet. DiskPress returns a separate file using native filesystem compression when eligible, leaving the original untouched. It is a normal file, not a ZIP archive.</p></div>
      <div class="ios-feature-grid two-up">
        <article class="product-card"><h3>Your compression rules still apply</h3><p>The action respects compression settings and exclusions. Unsupported or already-compressed contents may produce an uncompressed copy. It does not replace the source or reclaim space from the original.</p><p>The output stays in DiskPress/Shortcut Results until you move or delete it. Keeping both files can use additional storage.</p></article>
        <article class="product-card"><h3>Where you save it matters</h3><p>Another app or storage provider may remove native compression when it saves or copies the output. The file remains readable, but those storage savings may not carry over.</p><p>Processing an input copy does not give DiskPress permission to optimize the original in a cloud provider or your Photos library.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="supported-files">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Made for files, not everything on your device</p><h2>A clear boundary.<br />Your local folders.</h2><p class="lead">The Files app shows many kinds of storage. DiskPress for Files works only with supported, writable local files on APFS that you grant it permission to access.</p></div>
    <div class="ios-feature-grid two-up">
      <article class="product-card"><h3>A good place to start</h3><p>Choose a supported folder inside "On My iPhone" or "On My iPad", rather than the top-level location itself. Mostly stable documents and completed project files are useful candidates.</p><p>Already-compressed files may save little or nothing. Eligibility also depends on the folder's permissions and the operations its provider allows.</p></article>
      <article class="product-card"><h3>Not a photo or video optimizer</h3><p>The app cannot compress or deduplicate your Photos library, iCloud Drive, other cloud or network providers, installed apps, or protected system and app paths. Your photos and videos in the Photos app are not processed.</p><p>Seeing an item in Files does not mean it is a supported local file. Downloading a cloud item does not make its cloud-provider location a supported target.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="safety-note"><strong>Keep an independent backup.</strong> Optimization rewrites files at their existing paths and adds storage writes. Prefer settled files over folders with constant changes. Verification and recovery checks help protect the work, but are not a substitute for a backup.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section comparison-section" id="platforms">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Same engine, different platforms</p><h2>One purpose.<br />Different ways to work.</h2><p class="lead">Both apps offer native compression, deduplication and optional cleanup profiles. Mac adds automatic folder monitoring and a CLI for compression and deduplication. iPhone and iPad use Apple Shortcuts for scheduled workflows.</p></div>
      <div class="table-scroll platform-comparison" role="region" aria-label="Mac and iPhone or iPad feature comparison" tabindex="0">
        <table>
          <caption class="sr-only">Features of DiskPress for Mac and DiskPress for Files</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">DiskPress for Mac</th><th scope="col">DiskPress for Files</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Compression and APFS deduplication</th><td>Yes, using the shared engine</td><td>Yes, using the same engine</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Cleanup profiles and keep rules</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">One-time work and saved locations</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Continuous folder monitoring</th><td>Optional recurring optimization</td><td>No continuous monitoring</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Automation</th><td>CLI for scripts and AI agents</td><td>Shortcuts actions on iOS 16+, with background folder actions and Compress File Copy on iOS 27+</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Command line and menu bar</th><td>CLI and menu bar controls</td><td>No CLI or menu bar</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Supported storage</th><td>Eligible local files and compatible external volumes</td><td>Eligible local files selected through Files, not photos or videos in your Photos library, cloud storage, or protected paths</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Where to get it</th><td>Mac App Store or Setapp, with the same Mac features</td><td>Separate iPhone and iPad App Store app</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="ios-feature-grid two-up platform-notes">
        <article class="product-card"><h3>Background work is not monitoring</h3><p>On iOS or iPadOS 26 or later, a run started in the app may continue in the background when the system allows it. On iOS 27 or later, Shortcuts can also run saved folders in the background. The system may stop the work or require an unlock.</p><p>You can schedule a shortcut in Apple's Shortcuts app, but DiskPress does not continuously watch folders for changes. There is no iOS CLI or menu bar mode.</p></article>
        <article class="product-card"><h3>The savings do not need the app</h3><p>Once optimization finishes, native compression and clone sharing keep working without DiskPress for Files running. Edits, copies, or replacements can change those savings.</p><p>Keep the files you want. Open them normally. No separate reader required.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <div class="ios-feature-grid two-up">
      <article class="product-card"><p class="eyebrow">Private by design</p><h2>Your device.<br />Your files.</h2><p>DiskPress for Files makes no Internet connections. No separate app account, no analytics, no telemetry, and no file uploads. Settings, permissions, Activity, and recovery records stay on your device.</p><p>You choose whether to share reports or pass files and results to a shortcut. Other actions in that workflow can have their own privacy practices. Website links open in your browser.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy-policy/#ios">Read the iPhone and iPad privacy details</a></article>
      <article class="product-card"><p class="eyebrow">Built for iPhone and iPad</p><h2>Familiar purpose.<br />A new home.</h2><p>A dedicated touch interface with live progress, saved folders, and Activity. The app requires iOS or iPadOS 14 or later and supported local APFS storage.</p><p>Shortcuts actions require iOS 16 or later. Continuation of an app-started run in the background requires iOS 26 or later. Background folder actions and Compress File Copy require iOS 27 or later. The same version requirements apply to iPadOS.</p><p>Made by <a href={DEVELOPER_URL}>Ighor July</a>, the developer of DiskPress for Mac. Standalone Mac purchases, Setapp access, and the Storage Saver Duo Mac bundle do not include this app.</p>{APP_STORE_AVAILABLE && IOS_APP_STORE_AVAILABLE && <p>Want all three apps? <a href={STORAGE_SAVER_TRIO_URL}>Storage Saver Trio</a> includes DiskPress for Mac, App Archiver for Mac, and DiskPress for Files for iPhone and iPad in one App Store bundle.</p>}<a class="text-link" href="/terms-of-service/#ios">Read the iPhone and iPad terms</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq-section"><div class="wrap home-faq-grid"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Before you start</p><h2>A few useful<br />answers.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/support/">Contact support</a></div><FaqList questions={iosQuestions} /></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap closing-section"><h2>Keep more of what matters.</h2><p class="lead">DiskPress for Files for iPhone and iPad.</p><IosDownload /><a class="text-link" href="/#mac-download">Looking for DiskPress for Mac?</a></section>
</SiteLayout>
